  "interpretation": [
    "Increasing order can contain an exactly worst-scale unit phase Q mod p=+-1 in genuine 451 instances; adjacent prime gaps do not prevent it.",
    "Maximizing the centered residue is not a valid substitute for controlling the orbit discrepancy or continued fractions.",
    "The oracle discrepancy-greedy order substantially lowers the finite cumulative proxy and is numerically compatible with O(m polylog(k)), but no ordering theorem proves this and no proved short-prefix merge has this proxy as its loss.",
    "The experiment therefore neither proves nor refutes an asymptotic block-average lemma. It kills the phase-size-only bridge and isolates two separate missing theorems: an ordering bound and a many-seed short-prefix propagation bound."
